¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÖThis evil people, which refuse to hear my words, which walk in the imagination of their heart, and walk after other gods, to serve them, and to worship them, shall even be as this girdle, which is good for nothing.¦layout ªlast_verse
„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚFor as the girdle cleaveth to the loins of a man, so have I caused to cleave unto me the whole house of Israel and the whole house of Judah, saith the LORD; that they might be unto me for a people, and for a name, and for a praise, and for a glory: but they would not hear.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŞTherefore thou shalt speak unto them this word; Thus saith the LORD God of Israel, Every bottle shall be filled with wine: and they shall say unto thee, Do we not certainly know that every bottle shall be filled with wine?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙñThen shalt thou say unto them, Thus saith the LORD, Behold, I will fill all the inhabitants of this land, even the kings that sit upon David's throne, and the priests, and the prophets, and all the inhabitants of Jerusalem, with drunkenness.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŸAnd I will dash them one against another, even the fathers and the sons together, saith the LORD: I will not pity, nor spare, nor have mercy, but destroy them.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ>Hear ye, and give ear; be not proud: for the LORD hath spoken.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÏGive glory to the LORD your God, before he cause darkness, and before your feet stumble upon the dark mountains, and, while ye look for light, he turn it into the shadow of death, and make it gross darkness.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¸But if ye will not hear it, my soul shall weep in secret places for your pride; and mine eye shall weep sore, and run down with tears, because the LORD's flock is carried away captive.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‡Say unto the king and to the queen, Humble yourselves, sit down: for your principalities shall come down, even the crown of your glory.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ›The cities of the south shall be shut up, and none shall open them: Judah shall be carried away captive all of it, it shall be wholly carried away captive.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙyLift up your eyes, and behold them that come from the north: where is the flock that was given thee, thy beautiful flock?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ£What wilt thou say when he shall punish thee? for thou hast taught them to be captains, and as chief over thee: shall not sorrows take thee, as a woman in travail?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙœAnd if thou say in thine heart, Wherefore come these things upon me? For the greatness of thine iniquity are thy skirts discovered, and thy heels made bare.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙvCan the Ethiopian change his skin, or the leopard his spots? then may ye also do good, that are accustomed to do evil.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ]Therefore will I scatter them as the stubble that passeth away by the wind of the wilderness.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙThis is thy lot, the portion of thy measures from me, saith the LORD; because thou hast forgotten me, and trusted in falsehood.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙNTherefore will I discover thy skirts upon thy face, that thy shame may appear.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÑI have seen thine adulteries, and thy neighings, the lewdness of thy whoredom, and thine abominations on the hills in the fields. Woe unto thee, O Jerusalem! wilt thou not be made clean? when shall it once be?¦layout ªlast_verse